 "notes": "Shark Fin Reef, a ridge of granite blocks in the southern Similans whose tops break the surface like fins: the swim-through, the mooring and the depths, with the main block 40-60 m across (IDC Phuket) and the ridge about 400 m long; the north side is a gentler coral slope at 15-20 m, the south side drops steeply to 30-40 m, and the usual dive crosses the ridge from the south side to the shallower north for pick-up. There is no OpenStreetMap feature for the reef: the origin is the divezone position, 2 km east-south-east of Island 3 (IDC puts the start one mile south-east of it), so the position is uncertain. The site coordinates (8.545, 97.645) were 4 km north-west, near Island 4.",
